  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Vulnerable Refugees and Host Communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, Bangladesh through Improved Access to Health, Protection, Shelter, Site Management &amp; Site Development Services, and through Enhanced Disaster Displacement Management at National Leve</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For the Rohingya people in Bangladesh, 2024 marks the seventh year since their mass displacement from Myanmar. In coordination with the Government of Bangladesh, the international community, including the International Organization for Migration (IOM), has been providing life-saving assistance to support the Rohingya refugees. Despite seven years since their mass displacement, the majority of Rohingya still heavily depend on international aid and the hospitality of the Government of Bangladesh. In this project, IOM is providing primary healthcare, shelter/non-food items, protection, communication with communities, and site management and site development services across the seventeen Rohingya refugee camps in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar under the Organization&#x2019;s area of responsibility. This is contributing to improved access to essential services, enhanced disaster risk reduction and ensures effective coordination mechanisms in the response.</narrative>
  </description>
